;; Multi-variable sweep — curated question set (Phase S0).
;;
;; The benchmark for `bb sweep:run` (and any future leaderboard tooling).
;; Each entry is a (config, query) row-driver for the sweep runner.
;;
;; Schema (all keys required unless noted):
;;
;;   :id                       string, kebab-case, stable across runs
;;   :dataset                  :digdir | :public-docs
;;   :query                    user-visible question (utf-8, Norwegian or English)
;;   :golden-chunk-ids         vector of chunk-id strings expected in retrieval
;;                              (can be empty for questions where we trust the
;;                              answer-pattern only — see :grounding-mode below)
;;   :expected-answer-pattern  regex string; a correct synthesized answer must
;;                              match. Use Clojure re-pattern flags inline
;;                              (?i case-insensitive, ?s dotall).
;;   :tags                     set of keywords; used for leaderboard slicing.
;;                              Pick at least one from each of: difficulty,
;;                              form, domain. See vocabulary in
;;                              digdir.sweep.questions/known-tags.
;;   :source                   provenance — where the question came from
;;                              :baseline | :exploratory | :public-docs-smoke |
;;                              :altinn3-stability | :new | :exploratory-rerank
;;   :grounding-mode           :chunks+answer (default) | :answer-only |
;;                              :refusal-expected
;;                              :answer-only ⇒ skip recall@k for this row
;;                              :refusal-expected ⇒ a correct answer is one
;;                              that admits uncertainty / declines
;;   :notes                    optional — why this row is in the suite
;;
;; Mutation discipline:
;;   - Adding new rows: append; never reorder (ids are stable references).
;;   - Editing a row's :query or :expected-answer-pattern: bump :id with a
;;     -v2 suffix so old leaderboards stay comparable.
;;   - Removing a row: leave a tombstone entry {:id ... :tombstone? true}
;;     so the validator can report "expected N questions, saw N-1".
;;
;; Counts (2026-05-22 v3 — dataset-mismatch cleanup):
;;    0 digdir-arsverk (all 5 tombstoned 2026-05-22; goldens belong to a
;;                      separate Digdir corpus not present on this DB —
;;                      verified via /api/debug/chunk in baseline-v0)
;;    5 public-docs-smoke
;;    1 altinn3-stability
;;   12 exploratory-rerank (systemuser × 4, authz × 3, broker REST,
;;                          correspondence, events, studio grouping × 2)
;;   13 new (authored, mostly :answer-only)
;;   ---
;;   31 total live + 11 tombstones

