  cases are deliberately hard — Phase D classified them as 'stable but
  rank>10' / 'marginal variance' / 'marginal one-miss' / 'always missed'
  — which makes them the *most* useful rows for distinguishing sweep
  configs (easy cases land at rank=1 regardless of config; we want rows
